acts. Contract [1], for 14,710 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [2], for 14,878.87 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the legal limit does not prove any wrongdoing. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate improper actions by officials or organizations.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the reason for the amount. Review contract [2] to confirm if the same service was bought in another month. Look at the distribution of contracts across different months to see if there's a pattern in timing.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["UpEMBA7xdvvs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","Qa%2FRRDTY9pVVkTabT%2FRM8A%3D%3D","J11Yl67snyB4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}